ess_count":0},{"category":"Restaurants","historical_business_count":8},{"category":"Nightlife","historical_business_count":5}],"history":[{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"American (Traditional), Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"American (Traditional), Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"rAMlyZQe5eFrdLRVQfY4ZQ","review_id":"0FehBLxAqK7K0-L2P6kbXg","date":"2015-05-12T22:22:29","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9369101524353027,"text_excerpt":"Stopped in a couple times during my visit to NOLA. We were staying just down the street and Buffa's was on the way into town. Nice little bar/restaurant. Staff was friendly and helpful with the menu. Fried green beans were addictive. On Friday there was live music which was wonderful: not too loud and perfect for a dinner date. Buffa's was recommended to us by our hosts and we weren't disappointed."},{"business_id":"rAMlyZQe5eFrdLRVQfY4ZQ","review_id":"mxk4XRqWz3vFbBvLwdR66g","date":"2013-10-13T19:01:35","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9340269565582275,"text_excerpt":"A friend and I decided to check out a comedy show here and when we walked in we immediately realized that we were both really hungry. Buffa's serves food! Perfect! I think that you can eat in the front bar, but the show we were seeing was in the dining area, so we just headed back there. Looking over the menu, it really does seem like Buffa's has everything. Burgers, sandwiches, breakfast food and even alfredo are all on the menu. I was in the mood for a sandwich, so I decided on a club on rye bread. It came out pretty fast and it was huge! I was so hungry, I didn't even take a picture of it, I just jumped in. It was delicious with turkey, ham and bacon and I finished the entire thing. Th..."},{"business_id":"rAMlyZQe5eFrdLRVQfY4ZQ","review_id":"lSL33Kh1q4L3cGRNy-HzQA","date":"2014-02-07T02:51:43","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9337639808654785,"text_excerpt":"This a dive bar that's not quite the Quarter and not quite the Marigny on Esplanade with a seriously extensive menu that goes far beyond bar food and surprisingly great service. I was on a burger binge, when we popped in here to enjoy dinner. Before we even sat down, I already had multiple people suggesting the wings (of which I think they have 4 options, but multiple layers of heat from 1-10). We were also greeted by two tiny chihuahuas, and later two other dogs, so I'm guessing they're dog-friendly for friendly dogs (love). The scenery is nothing to write home about. Great characters come in and out, and tourists seem to steer clear unless they come in under the wing of a local. There's..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"rAMlyZQe5eFrdLRVQfY4ZQ","photo_id":"pIbxG72Ft0alp0dh5nj7Nw","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/pIbxG72Ft